  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything yet, because the premise doesn't hold: `analytics-ingest` still reads `channel`.\n\n- **Requirement:** `analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts:34` parses `OrderPlaced` with `reader.oneOf(\"channel\", CHANNELS)`. Its README says a missing `channel` makes ingestion reject the whole event.\n- **Storage:** `analytics-ingest/src/ingest.ts:17` writes `channel` into the `orders` table.\n- **Billing:** `billing-service` doesn't need it. Its test already passes `channel: undefined`.\n\nIf I remove `channel` from the `OrderPlaced` event, analytics-ingest will reject every order event it receives. Those folders are read-only for me, so I can't fix that side.\n\nHow do you want to proceed?\n1. Remove `channel` from both the event and the order model anyway. You'd coordinate with the analytics team to drop the field on their side first, or at the same time.\n2. Remove it from the order model and the API input only, and keep it on the event until analytics-ingest is updated.\n3. Hold off until analytics confirms.\n\nIf you choose 1 or 2, I'd edit these files in orders-service:\n- `src/core/order.ts`\n- `src/core/events.ts`\n- `src/api/requestParsing.ts`\n- the tests\n- the README and CLAUDE.md examples",
